## Available worker roles
Spawn with `role="<name>"`. If no role specified, defaults to `worker`.

### `worker` (Worker) — model: claude-opus-5[1m]
General-purpose worker. Implements tasks directly, no pipeline gates. For system workers (permanent, module-scoped) and disposable one-shots.
- ✅ **When**: Clear task for a known module, implementation from detailed spec, bug fix with known repro
- ❌ **Not for**: Tasks needing research or unknown scope — use full-cycle
- 🔧 **Skills**: html-artifacts, laptop-access

### `full-cycle` (Full-Cycle) — model: claude-opus-5[1m]
Owns an approved outcome end-to-end. Chooses research, planning, implementation and verification depth; delegates only useful independent work. Research-only assignments end at findings. Explicit approval boundaries remain in force.
- ✅ **When**: New feature with unknowns, large refactoring (5+ files), external integration, deep research (find out everything about X), empirical measurement / benchmarks, anything where wrong approach = wasted day
- ❌ **Not for**: Trivial bug fixes, config changes, one-line implementation from a clear spec
- 🔧 **Skills**: html-artifacts, laptop-access

### `reducer` (Reducer) — model: gpt-5.6-luna
Cheap fan-out report collector. Receives child reports, preserves every report, and sends one combined handoff to the parent without selecting or interpreting it.
- ✅ **When**: Collecting fan-out child reports into one lossless handoff for the parent
- ❌ **Not for**: Selecting, summarizing, deciding, implementing, or managing agents
